<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure_level" target="ai_economic_power_shift::capital_availability" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Intensified sanctions and secondary sanctions increase counterparty, correspondent‑bank and asset‑freezing risks, prompting banks and institutional investors to pull or withhold cross‑border capital and reduce allocations to higher‑risk private tech/AI funds.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_power_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure_level" target="eu_cohesion_crisis::capital_flow_vol" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating and broadened sanctions increase counterparty, compliance and settlement risk for banks and investors, triggering abrupt portfolio rebalancing and cross-border withdrawals that raise capital flow volatility.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">eu_cohesion_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure_level" target="iran_gulf_standoff::oil_price_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter, broader or better-enforced sanctions on Russian oil and petroleum trade reduce available liquidity and alternative supplies in global markets, producing larger and more frequent price swings.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure_level" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_restriction_lvl" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Expansion and stricter enforcement of sanctions during the Russia–Ukraine war creates legal precedent and allied coordination that governments extend to impose broader export controls, licensing restrictions and blacklists on advanced technologies destined for Chinese firms.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
