<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_restriction_lvl" target="ai_economic_power_shift::compute_capacity_demand" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export controls on high‑end accelerators and related equipment constrain shipments to foreign buyers and induce procurement deferrals, directly lowering short‑term aggregate demand for data‑centre and cloud compute capacity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_power_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_restriction_lvl" target="eu_cohesion_crisis::capital_flow_vol" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Wide-ranging export controls on critical technologies force corporates and funds to abruptly reallocate, cancel deals and pause cross-border projects, generating stop-start investment patterns and spikes in cross-border capital flow volatility.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">eu_cohesion_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_restriction_lvl" target="eu_cohesion_crisis::energy_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Targeted export limits on advanced components (e.g., cells, inverters, control electronics) raise procurement and replacement costs for EU renewable and storage projects, tightening supply of low‑cost energy alternatives and putting upward pressure on energy prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">eu_cohesion_crisis</data>
</edge>
