<edge source="eu_cohesion_crisis::fiscal_space" target="ai_economic_power_shift::ai_investment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Shrinking fiscal space forces governments to scale back R&amp;D grants, public procurement and co‑investment programs that directly seed and accelerate AI projects, reducing the pace of AI investment.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">eu_cohesion_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_power_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eu_cohesion_crisis::fiscal_space" target="iran_gulf_standoff::maritime_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased EU fiscal space enables additional defense and expeditionary funding (naval escorts, allied tasking, sanctions enforcement), directly raising the cost to Iranian actors of maritime interdiction and thereby reducing attack incidence.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">eu_cohesion_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eu_cohesion_crisis::fiscal_space" target="russia_ukraine_war::state_private_coord" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Shrinkage of fiscal space forces EU governments to cut or delay defense procurement, joint programs and subsidies, directly reducing the frequency and depth of operational coordination and information-sharing with private defense and logistics firms supporting Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">eu_cohesion_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eu_cohesion_crisis::fiscal_space" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_restriction_lvl" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Constrained EU fiscal space reduces governments' ability to subsidize strategic sectors, pushing them to prioritize inward investment and short‑term growth incentives by loosening export controls on certain dual‑use tech to attract capital, thereby lowering export restriction levels relevant to the US–China tech contest.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">eu_cohesion_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
